\* Generated by formal/plx_formal.py from the ParallaXReplay tables.
\* Do not edit by hand. Run: python3 formal/plx_formal.py emit
\*
\* ReplayInsertOutcome for protection-off and one slot: expiry clears the slot; stale and future skew cannot be replay; clash is not CacheFull.
\*
\* Safety claims (states and steps that must be unreachable):
\*   OffStoresNothing: protection off reports an insert and never occupies the slot
\*   SlotIsPaired: a stored handshake is one of the two abstract identities, or the slot is empty
\*   InsertRecordsTheCandidate: an insert writes the candidate into the slot
\*   StaleIsNotAReplay: a stale candidate is Stale, including when its nonce is already stored
\*   StaleCannotTakeReplay: a past-window or future-skewed timestamp is not classified as Replayed
\*   PastAndFutureAreStale: once decided, a past-window or +6s timestamp is Stale
\*   EdgeAndSkewAreFresh: the window edge and a future skew of +5 are fresh, so a stored nonce is Replayed
\*   ReplayDoesNotRecord: a replay reports Replayed, does not write, and only hits an occupied slot
\*   ClashIsNotFull: a transcript clash is Replayed, not CacheFull
\*   FullDoesNotEvict: CacheFull leaves the occupant in place and does not store the distinct candidate
\*   ProtectionOffIsInsert: with protection off the only decision is Inserted
\*   ExpireClearsTheSlot: pruning an expired entry deletes it and rebuilds an empty slot

---- MODULE ParallaXReplay ----
EXTENDS Integers

VARIABLES prot, slot_n, slot_t, scene, last, cand_n, stored, kind, pruned, n

